Raw-position `Prelude.fix` (function/proof/index result) was
withdrawn 2026-07-25 (audit finding S-2). Its contract,
`saw_fix_unique_exists_raw`, states uniqueness among all fixed
points — purely EXTENSIONAL, so it cannot observe SAW's operational
divergence and is honestly dischargeable for fixes whose SAW meaning
is bottom (witness: `fix Nat (\(n : Nat) -> mulNat n 0)`, provable in
three tokens while SAW's `mulNat` recurses on its first argument).

No checker hardening can catch this — every gate goes green — so the
emitter now rejects instead. Restoration path is the
productivity-gated raw contract in the 0.03 fragment-semantics
programme, matching what the wrapped Class-F/Class-S fixes have.
